    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood grew along the ancient Mississippi River ridges, a natural feature that guided its layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.seventhreedistilling.com/seven-three-blog/gentilly-neighborhood-through-the-ages"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dillard University, founded in 1935, became a hub for Black intellectual life and civil rights activism in Gentilly.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.seventhreedistilling.com/seven-three-blog/gentilly-neighborhood-through-the-ages"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pontchartrain Park, built in the 1950s, was the first suburban subdivision created specifically for middle‑class African Americans in New Orleans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.seventhreedistilling.com/seven-three-blog/gentilly-neighborhood-through-the-ages"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hurricane Katrina’s levee failures in 2005 flooded Gentilly up to 8 feet, causing widespread displacement.",
